---
/**
 * TERMS OF SERVICE. A template. Have a lawyer review it before you rely on it.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const updated = 'August 30, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`Terms governing the use of the ${SITE.legalName} website and software.`}
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow={`Last updated ${updated}`}
    title="Terms of Service"
    lead={`These terms govern your use of this website and of software published by ${SITE.legalName}.`}
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-8">
    <div class="legal">
      <h2>Acceptance</h2>
      <p>
        By using this website or any application published by {SITE.legalName},
        you agree to these terms. If you do not agree with them, please do not
        use the site or our software.
      </p>

      <h2>Use of the website</h2>
      <p>
        You may browse and use this website for lawful purposes. You may not
        attempt to gain unauthorised access to it, interfere with its operation,
        or use automated systems in a way that places an unreasonable load on
        our infrastructure.
      </p>

      <h2>Software licences</h2>
      <p>
        Applications distributed through an application store are licensed to
        you, not sold, under the terms presented at the point of download,
        together with any end user licence agreement that the store requires.
        You may not decompile, reverse engineer or redistribute our software
        except to the extent that applicable law expressly permits it.
      </p>

      <h2>Client work</h2>
      <p>
        Software and services we build for a client are governed by the separate
        written agreement with that client. Nothing on this page replaces or
        modifies such an agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        All content on this website, including text, design, graphics, code and
        the {SITE.name} name and logo, is the property of {SITE.legalName} and is
        protected by copyright and trademark law. Nothing on this site grants you
        a licence to use those marks.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to keep this website and our services available, but we do not
        guarantee uninterrupted access. We may modify, suspend or discontinue
        any part of the site or a product at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p>
        This website and our software are provided as is and as available,
        without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including
        but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
        particular purpose and non infringement, to the maximum extent permitted
        by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.legalName} shall not be liable
        for any indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages, or for any
        loss of data or profits, arising out of your use of this website or our software.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Colorado, United
        States, without regard to its conflict of law provisions.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top of this
        page shows when they were last revised. Continued use of the site after
        a change means you accept the revised terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can be sent to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
